            <ArticleTitle>Primary bilateral intrapelvic hydatid cyst presenting with adnexal cystic mass: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>694-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Hydatid disease, caused by Echinococcus granulosus, is a common parasitic infection of the liver. Disseminated intra-abdominal hydatid disease may occur with the rupture of the hydatid cyst into the peritoneal cavity, producing secondary echinococcosis. But primary hydatid cyst in the pelvis is rare. We report a case of bilateral hydatid cyst of the pelvis in a 53 years old woman presented with adnexal cystic mass.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
